# layout module

The `layout` module groups input sections, assigns addresses, builds segments, and accounts for sizes.

## Types

### `InputSection`

Normalized input section.

Fields:

- `name`: original section name.
- `data`: raw bytes, empty for NOBITS.
- `alignment`: required alignment.
- `is_alloc`, `is_writable`, `is_executable`, `is_nobits`: section flags.
- `file_index`: input file index.
- `section_index`: section index in the source object.

### `OutputSection`

Merged output section.

Fields:

- `name`: canonical name.
- `members`: input sections merged into it.
- `alignment`: maximum member alignment.
- `size`: total size after merging.
- `virtual_address`: final virtual address.
- `file_offset`: final file offset.
- `is_alloc`, `is_writable`, `is_executable`, `is_nobits`: flags.

Methods:

- `deinit(self, allocator)`: free the name and members.

### `SegmentFlags`

ELF-style protection flags.

Constants: `R = 4`, `W = 2`, `X = 1`.

### `Segment`

Loadable segment.

Fields:

- `virtual_address`, `file_offset`, `file_size`, `memory_size`, `alignment`, `flags`, `section_indices`.

Methods:

- `deinit(self, allocator)`: free section indices.
- `isReadable`, `isWritable`, `isExecutable`: check flags.
- `isCongruent(self)`: check `p_vaddr` and `p_offset` congruence.

### `SegmentSize`

Per-segment size breakdown.

Fields: `index`, `file_size`, `memory_size`, `bss_size`, `virtual_address`, `file_offset`.

### `SizeReport`

Aggregate image size report.

Fields: `total_file_size`, `total_memory_size`, `virtual_end`, `file_end`, `segments`.

### `Layout`

Section layout engine.

Fields include sections, segments, allocator, base address, page size, and address overrides.

Methods:

- `init(allocator, base_address, page_size)`: create a layout.
- `deinit(self)`: free all data.
- `count(self)`: number of output sections.
- `get(self, name)`: find an output section by name.
- `addInput(self, input)`: group an input section.
- `pinOutput(self, out_name, address)`: pin an output section at an address.
- `computeAddresses(self)`: assign virtual addresses and file offsets.
- `virtualSize(self)`: total virtual size.
- `fileSize(self)`: total file size.
- `segmentCount(self)`: number of segments.
- `buildSegments(self)`: build PT_LOAD-style segments.
- `accountSizes(self)`: finalize sizes and return a `SizeReport`.
- `freeSizeReport(self, report)`: free a report.

### `Error`

Error set for layout.

Values: `OutOfMemory`, `EmptyName`, `PinConflict`.

## Functions

- `canonicalizeName(name)`: collapse section names such as `.text.foo` to `.text`.
- `alignTo(value, alignment)`: align a value up to a power-of-two alignment.

## Example

```zig
var layout = sibl.Layout.init(allocator, 0x400000, 4096);
defer layout.deinit();

try layout.addInput(.{
    .name = ".text",
    .data = code,
    .alignment = 16,
    .is_alloc = true,
    .is_writable = false,
    .is_executable = true,
    .is_nobits = false,
    .file_index = 0,
});

layout.computeAddresses();
try layout.buildSegments();
var report = try layout.accountSizes();
defer layout.freeSizeReport(report);
```

## Notes

- Call `computeAddresses` before `buildSegments`.
- Call `buildSegments` before `accountSizes`.
- Protection changes between sections trigger page alignment.
- `.bss` contributes to memory size but not file size.
- `pinOutput` on the same section with a different address returns `PinConflict`.
- Canonicalization keeps `.data.rel.ro` distinct.
